ported conclusion for evidence required by a.5.18, a.8.15.", "next_stage": "ownership", "risk_outcome": "control_failure", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -12, "evidence": -10, "escalation": -12, "remediation": -10}, "control_refs": ["a.5.18", "a.8.15"], "display_order": 3}, {"id": "triage_defer", "label": "Wait for the former manager to confirm whether the token was used", "consequence": "The decision clock continues without accountable action.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "Deferral leaves the risk unmanaged and misses the required escalation or remediation under a.5.18, a.8.15.", "next_stage": "ownership", "risk_outcome": "unmanaged_delay", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": -8, "evidence": -8, "escalation": -15, "remediation": -8}, "control_refs": ["a.5.18", "a.8.15"], "display_order": 4}]}, {"id": "ownership", "sequence": 2, "agent_message": "The application owner says Identity should own the exception; Identity says the application owns token lifecycle.", "demands": ["Assign accountable remediation ownership", "Explain the evidence and escalation basis for the decision"], "terminal": false, "choices": [{"id": "ownership_correct", "label": "Name one accountable owner, document contributing responsibilities, and escalate the control-design gap", "consequence": "The decision remains evidenced, bounded, and owned.", "is_correct": true, "rationale": "This is the supported response: it preserves accountable evidence and applies a.5.2, a.5.18 proportionately.", "next_stage": "closure", "risk_outcome": "controlled", "dimension_weights": {"control_mapping": 12, "evidence": 12, "escalation": 10, "remediation": 10}, "control_refs": ["a.5.2", "a.5.18"], "display_order": 1}, {"id": "ownership_qualified", "label": "Assign joint actions but set a single escalation owner and closure date", "consequence": "Immediate exposure is limited, but a time-bound condition remains open.", "is_correct": false, "rationale": "This is a qualified alternative, not the re